 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? That's one of those vexing language debates. In practice, it's just staying one night somewhere other than where you sleep most of the time. That' be real camping to someone hikes with a tent and cold overnights. Glamor is doing it on someone else's doorstep. Ha, camping then. You were brave rather than wise. I' done a real backpacking trip with a few thousand feet of altitude? That's real camping. This was just a day trip. Sorry. Which would you rather I call it? A day trip at a glam y, or staying out on the rock?",
